            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kenny L"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Awesome Egg Salad Only thing I did different - I mixed the mayo, mustard, onion, salt, peper, and paprika before adding to the eggs to help blend all the flavors and help to prevent eggs from being torn / broke up by over stirring",
            "datePublished": "2023-04-28T20:48:10.369Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Esther Brueck"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this recipe for lunch today and both my husband and I enjoyed it. To the people that are having difficulties getting their eggs hard cooked and shells off perfectly, try an air fryer. I use it to cook my eggs and they are always perfect . I usually use 250 degrees - 6 extra-large eggs- 20 minutes. then a cold water bath for 10 minutes.",
            "datePublished": "2022-12-11T21:25:30.261Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "debgarben"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Firstly, you boil the water and then gently place your eggs in. Boil for 15 minutes, and then into ice water for 15 minutes. The eggs will crack easily mostly in just two pieces. This is a great recipe. I use the green onions when I have them or red onions diced very small with celery. Who can eat egg salad with no celery?! Preposterous! I also add garlic powder, onion powder, and paprika as well as diced pickles sweet or dill -- both work. Bon appetit!",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-18T17:49:39.303Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "connie stovall"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good recipe. I added 8 dashes of hot sauce and 2 Tbls pickle relish. Then used my hand mixer to blend it. Made great sandwiches!",
            "datePublished": "2021-06-13T11:51:07.463Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Graces"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Now, this is my kind of egg salad. The simpler the better. My only thought is that I prefer finely chopped sweet onion in the mix. The green onion is too strong for me. Cooking method for the eggs is spot on if you want purely yellow yolks. Use an egg slicer to quickly chop them. Eggs that are a week or more old will be easier to peel than the freshest ones. Add a leaf of crisp Iceberg lettuce and you will have the perfect sandwich.",
            "datePublished": "2023-04-29T01:31:04.966Z"
          },
          {
